# Elementary rigidity for Goldschmidt triples

F.6.12 excludes invariant and characteristic subgroups of a local core
normal in its product with the opposite residual. F.6.14 identifies the
small Sylow alternatives when the ambient two-residual is the odd core.
Both results preserve intrinsic subgroup conditions and ambient embeddings.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
§F.6, printed p.307 (1 March 2004 manuscript).
-/
